\description{
Evaluates six portfolio construction methods in a walk-forward
out-of-sample (OOS) backtest, focusing on \strong{weight stability} and OOS
performance. For each rolling training window (periods 1 through t), each
method's portfolio weights are computed and applied to the \strong{next period's}
(t+1) realised returns to produce an OOS portfolio return.

The diagnostic tests the central claim of the MVO-breakdown literature:
plug-in mean-variance (raw MVO) is an \emph{error maximiser} that amplifies
estimation noise in expected returns, producing high turnover, concentrated
positions, and poor OOS Sharpe. Regularised alternatives (GMV, shrunk-mu,
Black-Litterman, HRP) are more stable.

\strong{Look-ahead discipline (mandatory):} weights are estimated exclusively from
data in the training window (periods 1 through t). The OOS return for each
origin t is the portfolio return at period t+1 — strictly the first period
\emph{not} in the training set. The function never reads \code{returns[t+1, ]} when
constructing weights. This mirrors the \code{alpha-decay-min-t+1} rule.

\strong{Methods compared:}
\itemize{
\item \strong{\code{raw_mvo}} — Plug-in tangency portfolio \verb{w ∝ Σ⁻¹μ} using \strong{sample} Σ
and \strong{sample} μ (the article's error-maximiser worst case). Fails
with high frequency when p ≥ train_window (singular sample Σ).
\item \strong{\code{gmv}} — Global minimum-variance \verb{w ∝ Σ⁻¹1} via \code{\link[=hd_min_var_weights]{hd_min_var_weights()}}
using a regularised Σ from \code{\link[=hd_cov_estimate]{hd_cov_estimate()}}. No expected-return input.
\item \strong{\code{shrunk_mu}} — Tangency portfolio using Bayes-Stein (James-Stein / Jorion
1986) shrinkage on μ via \code{\link[=hd_returns_shrink]{hd_returns_shrink()}} with \code{method = "james_stein"}
and a regularised Σ. Documented method choice: \code{"james_stein"} (data-driven
shrinkage intensity, no tuning required).
\item \strong{\code{black_litterman}} — Tangency portfolio from the Black-Litterman (1992)
posterior μ̂ and Σ\_BL using \code{\link[=hd_black_litterman]{hd_black_litterman()}}. No investor views
(P = NULL); posterior collapses to the equilibrium prior Π = λ·Σ·w\_mkt.
Documented defaults: \code{w_mkt = 1/p} (equal weight) and \code{risk_aversion = 2.5}.
Theoretical result: BL with equal w\_mkt and no views yields approximately
equal-weight tangency weights (Σ\_BL⁻¹Π ∝ w\_mkt).
\item \strong{\code{equal_weight}} — 1/N portfolio (the robust benchmark). Zero turnover
by construction.
\item \strong{\code{hrp}} — Hierarchical Risk Parity via \code{\link[=hrp_weights]{hrp_weights()}}. Diversification
without expected-return estimation.
}
